---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Fossils Page Help">
    <section class="fossils-section">
        <h2 class="text-teal-400 my-1.5">Fossils Page Help</h2>
        <div>
            <p>
                Delving into the Fossils page, this section is designed to provide you with detailed information about the fossils found in the area you're
                exploring. The page is structured to give you insights into the types of fossils, their geological context, and their significance in
                understanding Earth's history. You can expect to find information on various fossil groups, their age, and the environments they lived in. The
                page may also include images and descriptions of notable fossil finds, as well as links to further resources for those interested in learning
                more about paleontology and fossil research.
            </p>
            <p>
                <img
                    srcset="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-local-dark.png&w=640 640w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-local-dark.png&w=1280 1280w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-local-dark.png&w=2048 2048w"
                    sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
                    src="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-local-dark.png&w=640"
                    alt="fossils page dark mode"
                    style="float: right; margin: 0 0 1em 2em; width: 300px; max-width: 40vw; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);"
                />
                This screenshot shows the fossils page of the app in dark mode. The image shows the local fossil records section, which provides information about
                the fossils found in the area you're exploring. The page is designed to be informative and visually engaging, with a focus on providing useful information
                about the fossils and their geological context. You can explore different fossil groups, learn about their age and significance, and view images
                and descriptions of notable fossil finds.
            </p>
            <p>
                Clicking on different fossil records will provide you with more detailed information about each fossil, including its classification, age, and
                the environment it lived in. You can also find links to further resources for those interested in learning more about paleontology and fossil
                research. The fossils page is a great way to explore the rich history of life on Earth and gain a deeper understanding of the ancient organisms
                that once inhabited our planet.
            </p>
            <p class="pt-15">
                <img
                    srcset="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-detail-dark.png&w=640 640w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-detail-dark.png&w=1280 1280w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-detail-dark.png&w=2048 2048w"
                    sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
                    src="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/fossil-detail-dark.png&w=640"
                    alt="fossils detail page dark mode"
                    style="float: left; margin: 1em 2em 0em 0em; width: 300px; max-width: 40vw; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);"
                />
                <p class="pt-8">
                    This screenshot shows the fossils detail page of the app in dark mode. The image shows the detailed information about a specific fossil,
                    including its classification, age, and the environment it lived in. The page is designed to be informative and visually engaging, with a
                    focus on providing useful information about the fossils and their geological context. You can explore different fossil groups, learn about
                    their age and significance, and view images and descriptions of notable fossil finds. The fossils detail page is a great way to gain a
                    deeper understanding of the ancient organisms that once inhabited our planet and their significance in understanding Earth's history.
                </p>
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
